        "evidence_anchor": "We found stand productivity gains of 7–53 % of mixed versus mono-specific stands continuing over the entire rotation. All mixtures achieved a 3–36 % higher leaf area index until advanced stand age. Stem diameter growth increased by up to 31 % in mixed stands. The growth efficiency of the leaf area was up to 31 % higher, except in mixtures of sessile oak and European beech. The trade-off between stem diameter growth and stand productivity was attenuated by the mixture."
